  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Naru vs State (2025:Rj-Jd:24812) on 21 May, 2025 Author: Farjand Ali Bench: Farjand Ali [2025:Rj-Jd:24812] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Revision Petition No. 880/2004 Naru S/o Udai Ram Jat aged 40 years, R/o Rolehera, Ps Chanderaia, District Chittorgarh (present at in sub jail Chittorgarh) ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan ----Respondent For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Sudhir Saruparia For Respondent(s) : Mr. Ss Rathore, Pp Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Farjand Ali Order 21/05/2025 1. 2. Briefly stated facts of the case are that the food inspector Mr. RS Pandey on 11.08.1887 spotted the petitioner while he was carrying milk with him.",
    "facts": "2. Briefly stated facts of the case are that the food inspector Mr. RS Pandey on 11.08.1887 spotted the petitioner while he was carrying milk with him. Samples were taken and sent to the laboratory. The complaint came to be submitted under Section 7/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act on the ground of report of adulteration in the food. The complaint came to be submitted on 26.04.1988. On 19.11.1988, an application was preferred on behalf of the petitioner under Section 13(2) of PF Act seeking re-analysis of the samples by the central laboratory. The said application was allowed and vide 12.12.1988 learned trial court directed to send the sample to central laboratory. Samples [2025:RJ-JD:24812] (2 of 3) [CRLR-880/2004] were received by CFSL on 21.12.1988. It was examined and then report dated 16.01.1989 was received. Based on the affirmation of adulteration by the central laboratory as well as the report of HLA regarding adulteration of milk the petitioner was convicted and sentenced the appeal preferred by him has also been dismissed, hence this revision petition. The core issue available in this revision petition would be that sample of milk was taken on 11.08.1987 and it was sent to central laboratory on 12.12.1988 and received on 21.12.1988 and till that time the commodity which is a perishable item must have been deteriorated which is a persumable fact.",
    "arguments": "Reliance can be placed on the judgment passed by Hon'ble Supreme Court in Girishbhai Dahyabhai Shah Vs. C.C. Jani and Anr. (2009) 15 SCC 64.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Reliance can be placed on the judgment passed by Hon'ble Supreme Court in Girishbhai Dahyabhai Shah Vs. C.C. Jani and Anr. (2009) 15 SCC 64."
  },
